  "id": "DrugBank_DB08826 - MONDO_17145",
  "verbalization": "Deferiprone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Beta-thalassemia And Related Diseases through a complex network of indications. The evidence suggests that Deferiprone is linked to Beta-thalassemia, which in turn is associated with Deferasirox, and Deferasirox is also linked to Beta-thalassemia And Related Diseases. This indicates a potential pathway where Deferiprone may influence the development or progression of the disease through its interaction with Deferasirox. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, including the involvement of Beta-thalassemia Intermedia and Luspatercept, further supports a broader role for Deferiprone in the context of thalassemia-related conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Deferiprone in the treatment or pathophysiology of Beta-thalassemia, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
